35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The public bed rates are straightforward, but whole-building lets are risky. Deposits are non-refundable, meaning the group pays for any late cancellations.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,Those inland centers sound like a nightmare. Eight people to a room with strict lights-out? That's not a training camp; it's a barracks.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,The public booking process is terrifying. A nine-page application and a lottery? And the cooking duty takes hours every day if the canteen is closed.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,Transport is our biggest variable. It can jump from 9% to 38% of the budget depending on the distance. We can't ignore that.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"I found out that the only time year-groups actually mix is during the evenings when everyone sleeps in the same place. Also, some people never even show up.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Misaki, the transport data combined with the non-refundable deposits makes distant, private lodges a huge financial gamble for the club.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, if we want them to mix, we need a shared space, but not a crowded one. The inland dorms would just make everyone grumpy.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shion, I agree. And @Asuka, the administrative burden of those public lotteries is just too much for the organizers to handle.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, if we avoid the lottery and the long-distance travel, we can keep the costs stable and the risk low.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, but if we stay too local or separate, we lose the chance to bond. We need a place where everyone stays together.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We have a conflict between the need for bonding and the need for financial stability. We cannot risk another budget shortfall.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,We also cannot risk the physical exhaustion of the members. Poor sleep ruins the final days of training.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,And we can't burn out the organizers. We need a system that doesn't require a nine-page application or hours of cooking.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"It seems we need a balance: low transport costs, simple booking, and a way to ensure we don't pay for people who cancel.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"But it has to be a place where we all sleep together, or the year-groups will just stay in their own circles.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
